# The variables are declared without a value, the text is read through a closure, and the marks are written behind the step. The loop of measures() is built twice. In front of its typed copy place and stop are asked for an int32; where that fails the other copy runs. place comes round as a parameter of the head, so no turn holds a test of it behind which the turn would have to begin again.
# f4 = measures
# -- source: typed-copy-of-the-loop-of-a-scanner-asks-for-its-variables-in-front-of-the-loop.ts
